//
// Every armour piece a player can be granted at character creation -
// feature 040, the four START WITH ... settings. FOUR TABLES, one per
// slot, in the game's own protectorCategory order: head, body, gloves,
// legwear, 33 / 34 / 26 / 31 rows summing to 124.
//
// The set is DERIVED, not listed: an EquipParamProtector row in that
// slot's category (offset 210), named by the game's own text, and
// wearable by both sexes (equipModelGender 3 at offset 209). The 21
// NOT NEEDED placeholders of category 4 are absent, so are the unnamed
// rows, and so are the Crown of Illusions and the Enlarged Head, which
// the game marks wearable by neither sex.
//
// EACH ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING, AND THERE ARE FOUR OF THEM:
// RandomizerDefaults stores each picker's selection as one character per
// row, positionally. Sorted by uppercased name, then ascending id - the
// id tie-break is what keeps each duplicate-name pair adjacent. A
// regenerated table in a different order silently remaps a saved
// selection onto a different piece of the same slot.
//
// TWO NAMES APPEAR TWICE EACH in the body table - HUNTER GARB and
// STUDENT UNIFORM - because the game gives two different rows each of
// those names. They are shipped as the game spells them rather than
// disambiguated with an invented word (plan 040 D1), and the generator
// asserts the duplicate set is exactly those two.
//
// `model` holds the armour id in DECIMAL, as a string, because the picker
// keys and logs on that field; the engine converts it with strtol. There
// is deliberately no second array of ids to fall out of step with this.
// `poolEntries` is 1 for every row: each row is exactly one piece.
//
// Names are FROM THE GAME'S OWN TEXT, uppercased, read at each exact id -
// never composed from an outfit prefix.
